      "body": "I've simplified the above example a bit, and it seems that the glitches happen in both cases, but sound differently:\n\n```\n(\nSynthDef(\\pulsar, { |out=0, amp=0.2, sustain=0.1|\n    var signal;\n    signal = SinOsc.ar(200) * EnvGen.ar(Env.sine(sustain), doneAction:2);\n    OffsetOut.ar(out, signal);\n}).add;\n)\n\n\n(\nb = Bus.audio(s, 2);\n{ InFeedback.ar(b, 2) }.play;\n\n\nPbind(\n    \\instrument, \\pulsar,\n    \\dur, Pgeom(0.00003, 1.01),\n    \\out, b\n).play;\n)\n\n\n\n// replacing the synth def with one that uses Out \n(\nSynthDef(\\pulsar, { |out=0, amp=0.2, sustain=0.1|\n    var signal;\n    signal = SinOsc.ar(200) * EnvGen.ar(Env.sine(sustain), doneAction:2);\n    Out.ar(out, signal);\n}).add;\n)\n```\n\nCertainly, the glitch disappears when using `In` instead of `InFeedback`:\n\n```\n\n\n\n(\nb = Bus.audio(s, 2);\n{ In.ar(b, 2) }.play;\n\n\nPbind(\n    \\instrument, \\pulsar,\n    \\dur, Pgeom(0.00003, 1.01),\n    \\out, b\n).play;\n)\n\n```\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
